WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.187
runKernel uses i to select the same position in input and output.

00:00:05.407 --> 00:00:10.164
The caller passes n as an element count and supplies separate GPU arrays.

00:00:10.384 --> 00:00:14.160
Every launched thread runs this body; the index chooses its data.

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:17.887
Read input[i].

00:00:18.107 --> 00:00:20.453
Choose an element using the thread index.

00:00:20.673 --> 00:00:21.761
Multiply.

00:00:21.981 --> 00:00:24.136
Apply the multiplier in runKernel.

00:00:24.356 --> 00:00:26.127
Write output[i].

00:00:26.347 --> 00:00:28.459
Keep the same destination index.

00:00:30.479 --> 00:00:33.593
The SM executes the threads in the assigned block.

00:00:33.813 --> 00:00:40.149
Threads are logical executions with their own values; they do not each own a physical arithmetic unit.
